{"The `end` variable is calculated using the same formula as `start` (both use `slotStartTime.hour()` and `slotStartTime.minute()`). This should calculate the slot end time using slotEndTime instead, causing incorrect validation of working hours as the end time check will always be identical to the start time check.": 0.979005753993988, "Comparing dayjs objects using the `===` operator will always return false because it compares object references, not the actual date/time values. Should use `.isSame()` method instead.": 0.9543795585632324, "Missing space after '//' in comment for 'check if date override for slot exists'": 0.097270667552948, "Missing space after '//' in comment for 'if no date override for slot exists check if it is within normal work hours'": 0.046163443475961685, "The call to `checkIfIsAvailable` is missing the `dateOverrides` and `workingHours` parameters. Unlike other calls which spread the user schedule object containing these fields, this call only spreads `availabilityCheckProps` which only contains `eventLength` and `currentSeats`, potentially allowing bookings at times when the user is unavailable.": 0.980143129825592, "No test was added to verify that date overrides are properly applied to fixed hosts in round-robin scheduling scenarios, leaving the main bug fix untested despite the PR description stating this should be covered.": 0.6830543279647827}